{% paidFeature feature="integrations" /%}

You can use Buttondown's [automations](/automations-introduction) to automatically cross-post your emails to social media platforms like Bluesky, LinkedIn, Twitter/X, Mastodon, Tumblr, and Arena.

## Setting up a cross-posting automation

[Create a cross-posting automation](https://buttondown.com/automations/new?trigger=email.send.started&name=Cross-post+to+social) to get started --- this will set the trigger and name for you. Click **Save changes** to create the automation, then open its settings page to add actions.

### Choosing when to cross-post

Two triggers can drive a cross-post, and the difference matters for large newsletters:

- **When an email starts sending** --- fires the moment the send begins. Your post goes up right away, no matter how long delivery takes. This is the default for the link above, and what most people want.
- **When an email finishes sending** --- waits until the last recipient has been delivered to. On a large list that can be several minutes, and the post won't go up before then.

A post that has already gone up can't be taken back automatically, so if you pause or cancel a send after it starts, remove the social post yourself.

### Adding social media actions

In the Actions section, click the action picker. You'll see the available social media platforms listed under their respective groups. Add one or more:

- **Create a Bluesky post** --- Requires Bluesky credentials in your [newsletter settings](https://buttondown.com/settings/integrations/bluesky).
- **Create a LinkedIn post** --- Requires a [connected LinkedIn account](https://buttondown.com/settings/integrations/linkedin).
- **Create a Twitter post** --- Requires a [connected Twitter/X account](https://buttondown.com/settings/integrations/twitter).
- **Create a Mastodon post** --- Requires Mastodon credentials in your [newsletter settings](https://buttondown.com/settings/integrations/mastodon).
- **Create a Tumblr post** --- Requires a [connected Tumblr account](https://buttondown.com/settings/integrations/tumblr).
- **Create an Arena post** --- Requires a [connected Arena account](https://buttondown.com/settings/integrations/arena) and a channel slug.

If a platform isn't connected yet, the action will appear disabled in the picker. Connect the integration from your settings, then return to the automation to add the action.

### Customizing the post content

Each social media action supports [template variables](/templating) for dynamic content. You can use:

- `{{ email.subject }}` --- The email's subject line.
- `{{ email.absolute_url }}` --- A link to the web version of the email.
- `{{ email }}` --- The full email object and its sub-variables.

If you leave the message field blank, Buttondown will use a sensible default based on the email's subject and URL.

### Timing

You can set each action to post **immediately** when the trigger fires, or add a delay. For example, you might post to Twitter right away but delay the LinkedIn post by an hour. Delays are measured from the trigger, so the same delay lands earlier under "starts sending" than under "finishes sending".

Click **Save changes** when you're done.

## Posting to multiple platforms

Since each automation supports multiple actions, you can cross-post to all your platforms from a single automation. Add one action per platform, each with its own timing and message content. There's no need to create separate automations for each platform.
